{% # theme-check-disable OrphanedSnippet, RemoteAsset %}
{% doc %}
  Placeholder-aware media emitter (WS-H). Mirrors PreviewService's isPlaceholderUrl()/
  phMedia()/PH_SVG (apps/web/app/services/preview/preview.service.ts:3430-3454) so a
  template's demo cdn.example.com URLs — or Shopify's own illustrative
  cdn.shopify.com/s/files/ library assets — never render a broken <img> on a real
  storefront. A merchant who hasn't replaced the demo image yet sees a tasteful
  accent-tinted placeholder glyph instead, exactly what the admin preview already shows.

  CLS restoration (binding follow-up to WS-H Task 5): width/height are OPTIONAL
  params, passed through to the real-<img> branch. Every call site across the
  renderer family now passes back the pre-a540c7a dimensions it hardcoded on its own
  bespoke <img> before this partial existed, so the layout-shift hint this partial
  briefly dropped is restored without expanding the partial's contract into
  per-archetype aspect-ratio knowledge — the caller still owns its own dimensions,
  it just hands them through instead of baking them into a caller-local <img>.

  Emission note: the width/height attributes are written UNCONDITIONALLY on the
  <img> tag (not behind an {% if width != blank %} guard) — Shopify's real
  ImgWidthAndHeight theme-check rule inspects the parsed HTML/Liquid AST for a
  literal width/height attribute NODE on the tag; an attribute wrapped in a Liquid
  conditional isn't recognized as present even when, as here, every real call site
  supplies a value (confirmed empirically: the conditional form flagged a real
  ERROR-severity offense against @shopify/theme-check-node even with 21/21 call
  sites passing width+height). An omitted width/height still degrades gracefully —
  browsers ignore an empty width="" / height="" exactly as if the attribute were
  absent — so this keeps the params genuinely optional in practice while satisfying
  the linter's static shape requirement.

  @param {string} url - candidate media URL (may be blank).
  @param {string} alt - alt/aria-label text.
  @param {string} css_class - class(es) the caller's layout expects on either element.
  @param {number} width - optional intrinsic width (CLS hint) for the real <img> branch.
  @param {number} height - optional intrinsic height (CLS hint) for the real <img> branch.
{% enddoc %}
{% liquid
  assign sa_media_is_placeholder = false
  if url == blank or url contains 'example.com' or url contains 'cdn.shopify.com/s/files/'
    assign sa_media_is_placeholder = true
  endif
%}
{% if sa_media_is_placeholder %}
  <div class="{{ css_class }} superapp-ph" role="img" aria-label="{{ alt | default: 'Sample image' | escape }}">
    <svg class="superapp-ph__glyph" viewBox="0 0 48 48" width="40" height="40" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="6" y="9" width="36" height="30" rx="3"/><circle cx="17" cy="19" r="3.5"/><path d="M8 34l10-9 7 6 6-6 9 9"/></svg>
  </div>
{% else %}
  <img class="{{ css_class }}" src="{{ url | escape }}" alt="{{ alt | escape }}" loading="lazy" width="{{ width }}" height="{{ height }}">
{% endif %}
